**Session 2 status — criteria not met; marker not written.**

This session closed one root-caused bug, made a decisive architectural call, and isolated the next blocker:

**Fixed and verified:** The run48 iunlink shutdown root — the B5 guard in `xfs_inactive` was skipping the *rightful freer* when a peer's transient PR pull demoted its EX and the one-shot re-acquire hit the DLM's blocked-upgrade contract (-EDEADLK). Run48's log had the smoking gun (`INACT-SKIP-STALE local_unlink=1 dlm_mode=3`, 5 leaked AGI bucket entries). Fix: honor the contract with an inline demote + re-acquire (the proven P60 pattern). Run49 verified: 7 fires, all recovered, zero leaks.

**Decision locked (Road B):** Per-op durability barriers on TCP stay OFF. With barriers on I measured the pace floor as structural — ~14.5ms per unlink (per-op ifree log_force+drain+flush) and 10-13ms per file handoff — best possible ~21.2s/round vs the <20s budget, across runs 51-59 of stage-timed analysis (P138 sa/sb/sc/sd split, P2D drain-why, P2G who-logs). Barriers-off runs at 8-14s/round with 2× margin. Along the way: leaf-provenance probes added, clean-REG release flush-skips (13.3→10.7ms/pull), mxfs now mounts noatime (verify-phase relatime was dirtying all 800 inodes per round), plus a stale-BAST-on-recycle reset.

**Open blocker (isolated in run61):** t6 hit *silent* `imap_to_bp rc=-5` sweeps over whole inode-cluster ranges at round 5 — no verifier print, no block-layer error, so the EIO is generated inside the mxfs read path — then diverged for 3 rounds until a cluster-wide dir wipe. Secondary: an all-node dir block↔leaf **format tear** on daddr 0x48 (XDD3 content under XDB3 expectation, the sess135 family). Two of my four new changes are already exonerated via modparams; noatime and the recycle-reset need a revert-bisect next.

Everything — findings, suspects, exact next steps (instrument the silent-EIO site at `xfs_mxfs_dlm.c:~12225`, bisect, then the format-tear root fix), and the unchanged ladder — is in ccmemory `sess2-END-road-b-barriers-off-t6-silent-eio-blocker`.

